{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be","id":1019299,"title":"How big can a Freehold be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-19T09:30:55-08:00","id":1019299,"title":"How big can a Freehold be?","content":"So I've been kicking around some Freehold ideas in my head, and I can't help but wonder how large a geographical area can be covered by a single Bulwark? Most Freeholds seem to encompass cities or metropolitan areas, but could they cast a wider net? Could multiple cities contribute to a collective Bulwark, thereby making them a giant Freehold? Could there be multiple layers of Bulwarks, where each city has its own, the cities within a state share in a larger, more complex ritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T10:30:19-08:00","id":1019323,"title":"","content":"And the questions keep churning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:49:16-08:00","id":1019372,"title":"","content":"There's a lot we don't know about how Freeholds operate in Second Edition. As a preliminary matter, the Freehold must exist within the boundaries of the &quot;story&quot; of the region. This will depend on the nature of the Courts, especially if the Courts are uniquely defined by the local environment (as opposed to broader Courts like Seasons or Directions). On consideration, is there a MINIMUM size for a Freehold, too? Could you have a King claim a bulwark the size of a room inside an apartment? And then, what you the geography is transient? What if the Freehold is a traveling circus or a caravan of some sort, with the bulwark coming and going with them? What if its a ship or a blimp? <br /> <br /> As a general rule, I would say whatever defining quest or agreement should in part reflect the overall space intended to be protected by the bulwark. Relatively simple for a small area, increasingly difficult the large the region. In theory you could even protect the entire world by completing a seemingly impossible task. Hmmmm....also, probably can't have a freehold within a freehold, one bulwark encompassing say a city block with another wraps around it to encompass the whole city. Although that would be interesting... And it brings up an interesting point. Could you usurp a freehold by fulfilling the obligations of your own bulwark while they were in the midst of fulfilling their own? Say a powerful bulwark takes a full day to fulfill, but you've crafted a less powerful story with a bulwark that can be finished within an hour. Could you make yourself king while the other bulwark had technically gone unfulfilled? I guess part of it depends on whether the warding power of the bulwark is able to stay &quot;on&quot; while it gets renewed. Anyway, back to the main topic...an area should probably have only one bulwark able to function at any given time. So to have a large area you'd need to pick a place far from other freeholds...or destroy those freeholds before you create your own larger one. Or maybe you could try to &quot;merge&quot; two stories from two separate freeholds into a new tale and quest to create a single united bulwark. That seems dangerous, though, and I imagine risks the destruction of both original bulwarks in the process. Also, crossovers tend to suck. If I was the Wyrd and I'd just seen the freehold version of Batman vs Superman....ugh. Fate would not be kind. Hurricanes would be involved. And volcanoes. And meteors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:33:42-08:00","id":1019511,"title":"","content":"Because of it's low-population but large size, I have that Australian Freeholds are much bigger than most other places in the world, aided by the distance warping of the hedge. For example, the Alice Springs freehold includes Engawala and Finke Gorge National Park within the far-reaches of it's area, meaning it covers more than 10,1788 square kilometers. That's a freehold which is around a third of the size of Germany, and yet will still have a very small population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-19-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:39:20-08:00","id":1019544,"title":"","content":"Unlike other gamelines, Changeling doesn't have a Tokyo freehold. It has a Honshu freehold. Yes, the freehold is over 228 thousand square kilometers (or 88 square miles), the size of a rather large island.<br /> <br /> I would say that freeholds could be any size, but that size needs to somehow be bound by some thematic limit other than just raw milage - city limits are one kind of boundry, an island's shores are another, a culture's reach a third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:43:12-08:00","id":1019546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1019544#post1019544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike other gamelines, Changeling doesn't have a Tokyo freehold. It has a Honshu freehold. Yes, the freehold is over 228 thousand square kilometers (or 88 square miles), the size of a rather large island.<br /> <br /> I would say that freeholds could be any size, but that size needs to somehow be bound by some thematic limit other than just raw milage - city limits are one kind of boundry, an island's shores are another, a culture's reach a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense. Thank you, this is an extremely helpful answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T03:16:53-08:00","id":1019682,"title":"","content":"I would say that Bulwark protects <b>particular</b> Lost, <i>not</i> the proper terrain. If yours Courts Story can sustain having changelings from all Honshu, all is it need is changelings following it. Mortals and other supernaturals are <b>not</b> protected under Bulwark self existing - they need to pledge allegiance to local Courts. This will make Courts more prominent and make Freeholds as large as you want - in reality is just 'oath of servitude to concept of our Bulwark that gives us protection', really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-20-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T03:49:49-08:00","id":1019689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1019544#post1019544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a culture's reach a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I kinda want to come up with a globe-spanning freehold based on McDonald's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:53:17-08:00","id":1019716,"title":"","content":"Yes! Now, would McDonald's be a Court, and other food franchises be other Courts, or are the Courts going be Dollar Menu, Sides, Drinks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T07:51:30-08:00","id":1019772,"title":"","content":"I keep coming back to an online based freehold but get stuck on the court particulars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:40:43-08:00","id":1019844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1019716#post1019716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! Now, would McDonald's be a Court, and other food franchises be other Courts, or are the Courts going be Dollar Menu, Sides, Drinks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was kinda thinking the Big Mac Court, the McNugget Court, and the Fry Court. I would also really want to tap those ancient wishful attempts at actually having characters that McDonald's used to do. Uh... here: <a href=\"http://mcdonalds.wikia.com/wiki/Category:Characters\" target=\"_blank\">http://mcdonalds.wikia.com/wiki/Category:Characters</a> WHY IS THERE A MCDONALDS WIKIA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:42:46-08:00","id":1019873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1019772#post1019772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep coming back to an online based freehold but get stuck on the court particulars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Court of White Knights, Court of Trolls, Court of Scholars... Titles could be Contributer, Moderator, Administrator, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:01:24-08:00","id":1020026,"title":"","content":"Look at the example Freeholds, they all tend to be extremely large. Honshu Freehold, Northern Michigan Freehold, Toronto (likely the whole GTA given the size and complexity of the Freehold and local enemy freeholds), Paris, Miami, ect..., none of these are small Freeholds, they massive. It makes sense that Changelings who usually lean towards large freeholds. In rural areas getting the population numbers high enough to have freehold would require the support of the changeling s of a vast area to make up for a low population, and in Urbane areas it would lead to constant turf war and less stability, stability which appeals to Changelings.<br /> <br /> Freeholds with small areas and small populations would find defending themselves rival Freeholds, True Far, other critters hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:28:22-08:00","id":1020045,"title":"","content":"I was still kicking around my nomadic Freehold idea. Maybe I'll get that done over the holidays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:45:34-08:00","id":1020057,"title":"","content":"I wonder how small a freehold could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:04:18-08:00","id":1020062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020057#post1020057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how small a freehold could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of population, the theoretical bare minimum is four Mantle 5 changelings in a two-Court system.<br /> <br /> In terms of territory, I wouldn't go smaller than a single high-traffic/occupancy building like a school or an apartment complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T00:19:16-08:00","id":1020213,"title":"","content":"Another point to consider is the age of the Freehold. At the time it was founded, my Austin Freehold stretched to the city limits. Today, it only encompasses the central downtown area. The city expanded over the years. A city like London now encompasses what were once a multitude of separate towns and villages. On a grander scale, imagine what happens if you create Freehold encompassing the borders of a nation that then ceases to exist because of conquest. Less dramatically, sometimes nations split in two or merge or simply alter existing borders via treaties or the like. So either the boundaries ebb and flow with the tides of history...or the boundaries remain unchanging and the Freehold comes to cross international or state lines. Maybe the Freehold even comes to represent from a narrative perspective the idealized lost nation of a people and time that only exists in the history books anymore. Might explain why Ireland, Scotland and England have varying legends of former rulers being overthrown and forced to live on in secret among the people. <br /> <br /> And on an even more dramatic scale of boundaries of islands and continents...well, myths aren't lacking in civilizations being lost beneath the sea or buried under impossibly destructive earthquakes. Imagine certain grim freeholds who decided it made more sense to keep the pacts of the Courts and the Bulwark of the freehold alive despite the extreme difficulties of living beneath the sea or underground or high in the mountains. Hell, some might even welcome the harshness as one more barrier the Gentry have to overcome to reclaim their former servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:27:05-08:00","id":1020344,"title":"","content":"It's also interesting how Freeholds grow as they gain in influence and power. The Scheherazade Freehold started with two immigrant Courts, absorbed the Changelings who would found the Ivory court and their Territory, then absorbed the Changelings who'd been trying to found a directional courts Freehold and their territory, then finally absorbed the Seelie and Seasonal Freeholds in the area, which formed the Silver Court, and their territory. I figure it just kept growing larger with population growth and conquest. Now not all Freeholds structures have that kind of flexibility, Seasonal Freeholds would likely try and fold conqueored Freeholds into preexisting Seasonal Courts, instead of encouraging them to form new Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:20:38-08:00","id":1020848,"title":"","content":"I dont think geographical limits are a &quot;thing&quot; one way or the other. Otherwise travel would he neigh impossible. A Honshu Changeling is protected by their Bulwark anywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> The reason centralized locations are prominent is because marketing / recruiting being easier and because that makes it easier to contribute to the Freehold's defense. You are also then near other people who have a vested interest in you being alive and contributing Mantle dots.<br /> <br /> A globe-spanning Internet freehold would be possible and cool.<br /> <br /> I could totally see a dark ages freehold based on the English Empire with a Bulwark surrounding the sun never setting on the empire and facilitating trade between colonies.<br /> <br /> In fact I could see Changelings facilitating the empire's expansion. One of the court's approaches being centeredon only getting attacks at night and them going &quot;I know what Ill do, Ill make sure its day in the empire forever.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:33:59-08:00","id":1020852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020848#post1020848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could totally see a dark ages freehold based on the English Empire with a Bulwark surrounding the sun never setting on the empire and facilitating trade between colonies.<br /> <br /> In fact I could see Changelings facilitating the empire's expansion. One of the court's approaches being centeredon only getting attacks at night and them going &quot;I know what Ill do, Ill make sure its day in the empire forever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Empire\" target=\"_blank\">British Empire</a> was in early to full Modern Era ( circa 1700-1990 ).<br /> 2. 'English Courts' are simple Seelie Courts - that are alliances of Spring &amp; Summer for Seelie and Autumn &amp; Winter for Unseelie. The same Seasonal Courts that Roman Empire created.<br /> <br /> It's all from 'colonialism reductionism' - American are 'rebel' British, THAT are 'rebel' Romans, THAT are 'rebel' Greeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-22-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T16:03:03-08:00","id":1021059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020852#post1020852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. 'English Courts' are simple Seelie Courts - that are alliances of Spring &amp; Summer for Seelie and Autumn &amp; Winter for Unseelie. The same Seasonal Courts that Roman Empire created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Toronto has both Seasonals and Seelie and Unseelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T20:50:19-08:00","id":1021128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020848#post1020848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think geographical limits are a &quot;thing&quot; one way or the other. Otherwise travel would he neigh impossible. A Honshu Changeling is protected by their Bulwark anywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> The reason centralized locations are prominent is because marketing / recruiting being easier and because that makes it easier to contribute to the Freehold's defense. You are also then near other people who have a vested interest in you being alive and contributing Mantle dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more complicated than that. The Hedge has <i>some</i> Ironside parallels, and it's warped by the Freehold's Bulwark, so there's <i>something</i> geographical going on, but it's quite undefined.<br /> <br /> Saying that travel is nigh-impossible under that interpretation is a bit of an overstatement. Travel would be <i>dangerous</i>, but you're still a member of your Court, and you've still got your own capabilities for fighting retreats and escapes. And it would be interesting to force Changelings to swear to a foreign Freehold for the duration of their stay: it speaks a lot to the point of fairy tale culture that hospitality still matters, that a guest does not harm his host, and a host provides shelter for his guest: a worthy Pledge if I ever saw one. It also compels some Changeling themes in that trauma survivors have legitimate justifications for why they don't want to go abroad, and part of what marks a healing person is their willingness to brave the unknown and, yes, still dangerous world.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd tell STs to change how it works based on the story they want to tell. Do they want visitors to be a big deal, or an unremarkable occurrence? Do they want a globe-trotting tale, or is the expedition Out There a terrifying adventure? I feel like 2e would work as well either way and there's no reason to demand it go one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T03:31:41-08:00","id":1021211,"title":"","content":"Yeah but if that was a global tradition I think it'd be mentioned somewhere. I'm not saying travel would be impossoble, just that its something the book would touch on.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, we only have betas and previews, so maybe it will be.<br /> <br /> I dont think swearing an oath to another freehold could be a thing under the riles we have, though. Oaths are explicitly permanent. You could never go back on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T08:01:38-08:00","id":1021276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021211#post1021211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oaths are explicitly permanent. You could never go back on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oaths are also explicitly as bound by their wording as any other pledge and we've been given nothing to suggest that the far more directly covered process of changing Courts requires Oathbreaker status.<br /> <br /> These are changelings we're talking about. An ironclad agreement with no escape clause is the sort of thing they fled from Faerie over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:41:18-08:00","id":1021305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021211#post1021211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but if that was a global tradition I think it'd be mentioned somewhere. I'm not saying travel would be impossoble, just that its something the book would touch on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already a global tradition. You won't find a culture in the world, older than thirty years, that doesn't have a tradition of hospitality. Including the old internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021211#post1021211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think swearing an oath to another freehold could be a thing under the riles we have, though. Oaths are explicitly permanent. You could never go back on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about, &quot;While in this freehold, I as guest will neither cause nor bring harm to the sworn Changelings within its bulwark&quot;? I'm too lazy to go back over the details of the system right now, but a time-based pledge seems like an obvious thing. Are Sealings equally permanent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:49:30-08:00","id":1021308,"title":"","content":"Sealings are temporary. Oaths permanently define a relationship and never getting out of them is a thing (except for Courts for some reason).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:06:29-08:00","id":1021312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021308#post1021308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oaths permanently define a relationship and never getting out of them is a thing (except for Courts for some reason).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: Wording. The connection lasts forever regardless of how its context changes, but there's nothing that indicates you can't join a new freehold just because you're already part of another one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:34:50-08:00","id":1021329,"title":"","content":"Also, I picked the wording I did pretty specifically. I built three loopholes in already:<br /> <br /> 1) You can walk away. If you're not in the Freehold, then it doesn't apply.<br /> 2) You can renounce guest-right. Gaiman's Sandman, Volume 4, has a lovely example of how that goes down.<br /> 2a) <i>Joining</i> the freehold formally also invalidates this clause. A resident is not a guest.<br /> 3) You can do what you want to anyone who <i>isn't</i> sworn.<br /> <br /> And that's without trying to be fancy, like quibbling over exactly what constitutes &quot;harm&quot; or proximate cause or the like. Can you really imagine a Changeling saying no to an Oath like that, without saying no to <i>all</i> Oaths, or a Freehold having special trouble demanding it from a visitor?<br /> <br /> And if Sealings are temporary, that's really all that's needed for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T11:33:05-08:00","id":1021347,"title":"","content":"Oaths permanently define a relationship, yes, but their terms don't have to be permanent. Using Errol's &quot;While in this freehold, I as guest will neither cause nor bring harm to the sworn Changelings within its bulwark&quot; example, there is nothing preventing you from leaving the Freehold. The Oath would simply define your relationship as a former guest of the Freehold, and the Freehold as your former host. Since the terms of the Oath don't define responsibilities for former guests/hosts, there's no problem. If you didn't violate the terms of the Oath, it doesn't define you as a person who betrayed the Freehold's hospitality, and you don't gain the Oathbreaker Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-23-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T11:47:19-08:00","id":1021354,"title":"","content":"@Charlaquin<br /> I am rather new to the forums because I used to be a lurker and am unsure of the courtoisie <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(excuse the pun)</span> involved, but I was curious as to whether directing people to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\">this thread</a> would be of any merit? It is an index I have attempted to start for homebrewed 2E Freeholds and Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T12:38:02-08:00","id":1021365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue-01.exe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021354#post1021354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin<br /> I am rather new to the forums because I used to be a lurker and am unsure of the courtoisie <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(excuse the pun)</span> involved, but I was curious as to whether directing people to <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds&amp;quot;]this</a> thread[/URL] would be of any merit? It is an index I have attempted to start for homebrewed 2E Freeholds and Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. I think the original question has been answered to my satisfaction, so at this point we're just talking about Freehold Theory in general, and a thread for custom Freeholds is as on topic as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T12:59:36-08:00","id":1021374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020848#post1020848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think geographical limits are a &quot;thing&quot; one way or the other. Otherwise travel would he neigh impossible. A Honshu Changeling is protected by their Bulwark anywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> The reason centralized locations are prominent is because marketing / recruiting being easier and because that makes it easier to contribute to the Freehold's defense. You are also then near other people who have a vested interest in you being alive and contributing Mantle dots.<br /> <br /> A globe-spanning Internet freehold would be possible and cool.<br /> <br /> I could totally see a dark ages freehold based on the English Empire with a Bulwark surrounding the sun never setting on the empire and facilitating trade between colonies.<br /> <br /> In fact I could see Changelings facilitating the empire's expansion. One of the court's approaches being centeredon only getting attacks at night and them going &quot;I know what Ill do, Ill make sure its day in the empire forever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait. You are saying that you can join a Freehold, then immediately travel the world with impunity while benefiting from the Bulwark of that Freehold with impunity and just need to turn up whenever the Bulwark need to be renewed? So....why have the Freehold at all, then? Why not just have a few ancient agreements scattered across the world that Changelings make pilgrimage to when the Bulwark needs to be shored up (and guarded by an appropriately stoic and powerful number of changelings to make sure the binding is protected)? I mean, isn't it actually safer for you if you run off to somewhere far from the Bulwark under this model? &quot;Oh, I'm sorry Mr. Huntman, but as you can clearly see you will need to go to the remote Mt. Fuckingtall in TImbuktu and survive the 40 trials of Falling on Pointy Things if you want to take me anywhere!&quot; Wouldn't the distance and difficulty of tracking them down be an extra hindrance under this model?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:51:33-08:00","id":1021436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021374#post1021374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait. You are saying that you can join a Freehold, then immediately travel the world with impunity while benefiting from the Bulwark of that Freehold with impunity and just need to turn up whenever the Bulwark need to be renewed? So....why have the Freehold at all, then? Why not just have a few ancient agreements scattered across the world that Changelings make pilgrimage to when the Bulwark needs to be shored up (and guarded by an appropriately stoic and powerful number of changelings to make sure the binding is protected)? I mean, isn't it actually safer for you if you run off to somewhere far from the Bulwark under this model? &amp;quot;Oh, I'm sorry Mr. Huntman, but as you can clearly see you will need to go to the remote Mt. Fuckingtall in TImbuktu and survive the 40 trials of Falling on Pointy Things if you want to take me anywhere!&amp;quot; Wouldn't the distance and difficulty of tracking them down be an extra hindrance under this model?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. First, Huntsmen dont have to follow approaches, they just get an advantage for doing so. It doesnt stop loyalists at all. A central government, military, and friends you can call up help with those things. It also helps with education and mortal world integration, and emmotional support, and on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:16:56-08:00","id":1021447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021365#post1021365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly. I think the original question has been answered to my satisfaction, so at this point we're just talking about Freehold Theory in general, and a thread for custom Freeholds is as on topic as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! I am not sure if bringing this up here is appropriate but, what about a freehold that exists within the hedge? I believe I've talked a little to ArcaneArts about it and he was very intentionally vague, but from my understanding a Freehold only requires only the sufficient number of changelings with dots in mantle.<br /> I find it interesting because in the fluff written for freehold creation it mentions that a bulwark is like imposing fae laws on reality, which got me to thinking, if some changelings <i>DID</i> make a freehold in the hedge with a bulwark, it would almost be like a true Arcadian domain where the bulwark itself is the local keeper as it imposes Arcadian laws on the already Wyrd run hedge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I am currently working on a setting based on this idea and will be posting it to my index thread if anybody is interested.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:51:40-08:00","id":1021452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue-01.exe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021447#post1021447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome! I am not sure if bringing this up here is appropriate but, what about a freehold that exists within the hedge? I believe I've talked a little to ArcaneArts about it and he was very intentionally vague, but from my understanding a Freehold only requires only the sufficient number of changelings with dots in mantle.<br /> I find it interesting because in the fluff written for freehold creation it mentions that a bulwark is like imposing fae laws on reality, which got me to thinking, if some changelings <i>DID</i> make a freehold in the hedge with a bulwark, it would almost be like a true Arcadian domain where the bulwark itself is the local keeper as it imposes Arcadian laws on the already Wyrd run hedge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I am currently working on a setting based on this idea and will be posting it to my index thread if anybody is interested.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my. This would probably have wonderfully disastrous results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T19:53:34-08:00","id":1021460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021374#post1021374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait. You are saying that you can join a Freehold, then immediately travel the world with impunity while benefiting from the Bulwark of that Freehold with impunity and just need to turn up whenever the Bulwark need to be renewed?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the freehold is founded on an appropriately far-reaching story and you can still be meaningfully said to be a Courtier of the appropriate variety, sure.<br /> <br /> Chicago's Wind Court has an entire freehold role that amounts to &quot;give changelings from outside of Chicago cause to stay in Chicago for a while,&quot; 1e provides ample precedent for &quot;foreign&quot; changelings with unusual Mantles to be curiosities rather than an open invitation to the Fae, and the Seasonal Courts are perennial favorites for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T21:32:16-08:00","id":1021471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021460#post1021460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago's Wind Court has an entire freehold role that amounts to &quot;give changelings from outside of Chicago cause to stay in Chicago for a while,&quot; 1e provides ample precedent for &quot;foreign&quot; changelings with unusual Mantles to be curiosities rather than an open invitation to the Fae, and the Seasonal Courts are perennial favorites for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally! I can have Dresden Files <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Mab\" target=\"_blank\">Mab</a> as Winter Queen high Wyrd example!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T00:05:30-08:00","id":1021486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021452#post1021452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my. This would probably have wonderfully disastrous results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes that is the intention, a freehold of half mad changelings whose freehold story is one of struggle.<br /> At least the first dot of mantle would have to give safe place OR hollow, with the second being absolutely hollow, where each dot is contributed towards the entire freehold (thus the only reason that they haven't been wiped off the face of the hedge)<br /> I'm still in very early stages of writing this and hesitant to reveal too much as I intend this to be part of an entire homebrew setting I am building for a current Chronicle.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T00:39:39-08:00","id":1021489,"title":"","content":"I think that a Changeling has the basic benefits of belonging to a Freehold/Court no matter where they go, but loose out on the more complex advantages like a hedge more suited to them, nearby allies, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T23:50:24-08:00","id":1021865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1021489#post1021489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a Changeling has the basic benefits of belonging to a Freehold/Court no matter where they go, but loose out on the more complex advantages like a hedge more suited to them, nearby allies, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to disagree to an extent, however I'm not fully versed in the rules for bulwarks and approaches yet. To my understanding changelings get approaches individual to themselves as well as benefiting from a more rigid system of fae law as imposed by the bulwark, granting them additional approaches while inside the freehold.<br /> <br /> I'd say that if dots in mantle gave you access to a certain merit, contract or skill dot, whatever the benefit, that they always apply regardless of whether you are currently in the bounds of your courts freehold or not, however this could be on an entirely case by case basis, dependent on the advantages given by the mantle. Resources is easily justified to keep, as is a skill dot or anything you can physically attain or accomplish, but the ability to rely on a retainer that is dependent on the freehold and mantle is harder to justify, just as with contacts or allies that are all likely within the freehold.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely right in saying that they lose out on complex advantages such as a hedge more suited to them, additional and more rigid approaches, a network of implied allies and any advantages granted that are tied to the Freehold intrinsically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:54:50-08:00","id":1022038,"title":"","content":"I read nothing that suggests approaches only function in the territory of your Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:58:07-08:00","id":1022529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be#post1019299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been kicking around some Freehold ideas in my head, and I can't help but wonder how large a geographical area can be covered by a single Bulwark? Most Freeholds seem to encompass cities or metropolitan areas, but could they cast a wider net? Could multiple cities contribute to a collective Bulwark, thereby making them a giant Freehold? Could there be multiple layers of Bulwarks, where each city has its own, the cities within a state share in a larger, more complex ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Canonically&quot;, Honshu is the biggest Freehold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1020057#post1020057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how small a freehold could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not mentioned in the core, but I have plans to talk about a Freehold with three members holed up in a single room in a war zone in one of the supplements. And Freeholds of three members are not remarkably uncommon, they just dissolve or recruit with relative alacrity in most cases. So, that'd be the smallest. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:18:35-08:00","id":1022599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022529#post1022529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Canonically&quot;, Honshu is the biggest Freehold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not mentioned in the core, but I have plans to talk about a Freehold with three members holed up in a single room in a war zone in one of the supplements. And Freeholds of three members are not remarkably uncommon, they just dissolve or recruit with relative alacrity in most cases. So, that'd be the smallest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any comment on the hedgehold I am working on?<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Expect a post about it soon.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T21:39:52-08:00","id":1022611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022529#post1022529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not mentioned in the core, but I have plans to talk about a Freehold with three members holed up in a single room in a war zone in one of the supplements. And Freeholds of three members are not remarkably uncommon, they just dissolve or recruit with relative alacrity in most cases. So, that'd be the smallest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Freehold creation section mentions a court needing 10 dots of Mantle to remain a court, however. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:02:14-08:00","id":1022616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022611#post1022611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Freehold creation section mentions a court needing 10 dots of Mantle to remain a court, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. So they all have to be at least relatively potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:03:38-08:00","id":1022617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue-01.exe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022599#post1022599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Any comment on the hedgehold I am working on?<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Expect a post about it soon.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read it. I'll take a look when I get a moment maybe. Super busy right now, so not in a critiquing mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:11:58-08:00","id":1022619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022616#post1022616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. So they all have to be at least relatively potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legume's pointing out that a three-member freehold is mathematically impossible without breaking the five-dot cap on Mantle, which is admittedly solved by the addition of one more Mantle 5 changeling and the stipulation of a grace period for rebuilding lost membership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:00:30-08:00","id":1022656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022619#post1022619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legume's pointing out that a three-member freehold is mathematically impossible without breaking the five-dot cap on Mantle, which is admittedly solved by the addition of one more Mantle 5 changeling and the stipulation of a grace period for rebuilding lost membership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a time restriction on purchasing Mantle? If so, I totally overlooked it, and should review it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:13:29-08:00","id":1022658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022656#post1022656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there a time restriction on purchasing Mantle? If so, I totally overlooked it, and should review it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that the Court Creation mechanics specify that a freehold survives as long as there are at least two Courts and a functioning Bulwark and then goes on to say that a Court generally collapses if it falls below ten dots of Mantle between its constituents \u2014 the material isn't worded in a manner that suggests this would not mean an immediate suspension of the freehold's narrative framework as soon as it lost a member in a freehold with a single-digit headcount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:43:15-08:00","id":1022776,"title":"","content":"To put it in other terms, if a Freehold needs at least 2 courts to be a Freehold, and a Court needs at least 10 dots of Mantle between its members to be a Court, you need at least 2 Changelings with 5 dots of Mantle each to form a Court and 2 such Courts to form a Freehold, making the minimum number of members for a Freehold 4. In a 4-member Freehold, if any one of the members dies or otherwise stops being a member, the Court loses 5 of its 10 dots of Mantle and no longer has enough Mantle to be consodered a Court. That means the Freehold loses 1 of its 2 Courts and no longer has enough Courts to be considered a Freehold. So, unless a grace period is added that allows a Court to replace a lost member, a 4-member Freehold won't be able to survive the loss of a single member.<br /> <br /> Which seems fine to me personally. Such a small Freehold should probably be extremely fragile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:07:11-08:00","id":1022786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022038#post1022038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read nothing that suggests approaches only function in the territory of your Freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is starting to sound like exactly the kind of thing we should ask the writers to clarify before the final release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:57:26-08:00","id":1022841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022786#post1022786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is starting to sound like exactly the kind of thing we should ask the writers to clarify before the final release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on it, but I would argue that the general direction is they work wherever so long as the freehold hasn't broken the Bulwark or the courtier hasn't lost their identity in the freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:59:42-08:00","id":1022843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022529#post1022529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not mentioned in the core, but I have plans to talk about a Freehold with three members holed up in a single room in a war zone in one of the supplements. And Freeholds of three members are not remarkably uncommon, they just dissolve or recruit with relative alacrity in most cases. So, that'd be the smallest.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trench&quot; Holds. I dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:23:25-08:00","id":1022993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022658#post1022658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more that the Court Creation mechanics specify that a freehold survives as long as there are at least two Courts and a functioning Bulwark and then goes on to say that a Court generally collapses if it falls below ten dots of Mantle between its constituents \u2014 the material isn't worded in a manner that suggests this would not mean an immediate suspension of the freehold's narrative framework as soon as it lost a member in a freehold with a single-digit headcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure. Gotcha. <br /> <br /> I'll probably adjust that down to ten combined dots amongst the Courts, not ten per Court. I could have sworn that's what it was initially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:24:14-08:00","id":1022995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022786#post1022786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is starting to sound like exactly the kind of thing we should ask the writers to clarify before the final release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll clarify, but they should work outside the immediate territory. Diplomats, for example, would be covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:35:43-08:00","id":1023102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1022993#post1022993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh sure. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> I'll probably adjust that down to ten combined dots amongst the Courts, not ten per Court. I could have sworn that's what it was initially.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you could have a freehold with a Court consisting of only have a single Mantle 1 courtier? Talk about king of an anthill. heh. Personally, I think 10 per Court makes sense. A court should usually be a bigger organization than just a motley or an individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T01:11:32-08:00","id":1023151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023102#post1023102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you could have a freehold with a Court consisting of only have a single Mantle 1 courtier? Talk about king of an anthill. heh. Personally, I think 10 per Court makes sense. A court should usually be a bigger organization than just a motley or an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mulling it over, I think a Court would need at least about a 3. I'd say you could have a Court with 3 and 4, and one with 3, and that'd fulfill the 10 required. I definitely want room for very small Freeholds, for the reasons mentioned above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:11:24-08:00","id":1023184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023151#post1023151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mulling it over, I think a Court would need at least about a 3. I'd say you could have a Court with 3 and 4, and one with 3, and that'd fulfill the 10 required. I definitely want room for very small Freeholds, for the reasons mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, the Bears' residence in Goldilocks could have been a micro-Freehold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:38:36-08:00","id":1023237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023184#post1023184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, the Bears' residence in Goldilocks could have been a micro-Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let's add the Three Little Pigs as well. The Courts are of Straw, Wood, and Brick. Their Approach involves letting two fortresses fall to the notorious Huntsman known as the Big Bad Wolf (casualties not necessary), then going all-out in the third fortress to pound the wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:38:38-08:00","id":1023238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023184#post1023184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, the Bears' residence in Goldilocks could have been a micro-Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:05:46-08:00","id":1023251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023237#post1023237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then let's add the Three Little Pigs as well. The Courts are of Straw, Wood, and Brick. Their Approach involves letting two fortresses fall to the notorious Huntsman known as the Big Bad Wolf (casualties not necessary), then going all-out in the third fortress to pound the wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>#BBWolfWasAnInsideJob?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:56:41-08:00","id":1023326,"title":"","content":"I have been told that the Three Little Pigs actually maps to a historical German political situation, but I have yet to successfully track the details down. (The author who made the claim doesn't remember where he got it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:08:00-08:00","id":1023329,"title":"","content":"I feel like mapping your approach too closely to one specific, well-known story should have consequences. If you haven't created the story yourself, you have less control over your role in it and the Wyrd may get even more Rail-roading. In other words, don't model your approach on one specific fairytale for the same reason that you don't name your Freehold New Lyonesse or the New Alamo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T14:19:41-08:00","id":1023424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023326#post1023326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been told that the Three Little Pigs actually maps to a historical German political situation, but I have yet to successfully track the details down. (The author who made the claim doesn't remember where he got it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... maybe the pigs represent farming, forestry, and industry? Agriculture and industry always clash when the latter starts to rise, but dunno about forestry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023329#post1023329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like mapping your approach too closely to one specific, well-known story should have consequences. If you haven't created the story yourself, you have less control over your role in it and the Wyrd may get even more Rail-roading. In other words, don't model your approach on one specific fairytale for the same reason that you don't name your Freehold New Lyonesse or the New Alamo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Wyrd probably gets its hooks on such daring freeholds.<br /> <br /> In other words, a story hook! (No, I''ll never be sorry for the pun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:22:42-08:00","id":1025564,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly seized by a desire to see what a freehold among the soldiers of a given firebase in Vietnam might have looked like, as part of a wider recent itch towards 1960s CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:26:12-08:00","id":1025566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1025564#post1025564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suddenly seized by a desire to see what a freehold among the soldiers of a given firebase in Vietnam might have looked like, as part of a wider recent itch towards 1960s CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>that definitely sounds like it could be interesting and fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:44:47-08:00","id":1025866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1023424#post1023424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Wyrd probably gets its hooks on such daring freeholds.<br /> <br /> In other words, a story hook! (No, I''ll never be sorry for the pun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't call them daring so much as unimaginative. But yeah, great story hook","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:49:47-08:00","id":1025869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1025866#post1025866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't call them daring so much as unimaginative. But yeah, great story hook</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for changelings, to be unimaginative <i>is </i>daring (and to be not paranoid is to give up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:31:16-08:00","id":1026296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019299-how-big-can-a-freehold-be?p=1025564#post1025564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suddenly seized by a desire to see what a freehold among the soldiers of a given firebase in Vietnam might have looked like, as part of a wider recent itch towards 1960s CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh. I would love to tie that to my Carthian material in Secrets of the Covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T21:38:42-08:00","id":1026312,"title":"","